WEBVTT

00:01.859 --> 00:05.867
[There is only one law in emotion:
to bring happiness to those we love.]

00:05.868 --> 00:12.007
[There is only one law in emotion:
to bring happiness to those we love.]
[Stendhal, diary entry dated June 19, 1805]

00:15.158 --> 00:17.848
This is remarkable, Professor Ayanokouji.

00:18.030 --> 00:21.200
Kiyotaka is clearly a prodigy.

00:21.400 --> 00:24.480
Being a natural-born prodigy is pointless.

00:25.190 --> 00:32.140
Don't forget that we can foster excellence
in anyone, no matter how inferior their DNA.

00:32.369 --> 00:33.540
Y-Yes, sir.

00:33.840 --> 00:37.530
Don't you dare show him any favor
just because he's my son.

00:39.030 --> 00:41.890
Even if it means you have to break him.

00:43.840 --> 00:46.400
How unusual of you, Arisu,

00:46.800 --> 00:49.400
to take such an interest.

00:49.830 --> 00:53.370
An experiment to artificially produce geniuses…

00:53.720 --> 00:56.010
could hardly escape my attention.

00:56.540 --> 00:58.810
You never change, do you.

01:00.050 --> 01:01.190
Who is that?

01:01.760 --> 01:05.209
Ah, that's the professor's son.

01:05.970 --> 01:11.920
I think his name is Ayanokouji Kiyotaka.

01:12.720 --> 01:16.240
Ayanokouji Kiyotaka…

01:18.400 --> 01:23.080
The final special exam of the year will now begin.

01:23.920 --> 01:30.680
Please select five of your class's proposed
events, and press the confirm button.

01:34.870 --> 01:38.640
I've been waiting for the day
I'd finally be able to take you on…

01:39.530 --> 01:43.020
And now, fate has finally
brought us to this moment.

01:48.290 --> 01:52.770
Fate, huh. You don't usually
speak in such conceptual terms.

01:53.360 --> 01:54.930
I am a lady, you know.

01:55.490 --> 01:59.140
Ayanokouji worked so hard to get to Class C,

01:59.200 --> 02:06.130
and he still has to go up against
someone like Sakayanagi. Poor thing.

02:06.170 --> 02:08.169
Keep your feelings out of this.

02:08.620 --> 02:10.080
My mistake!

02:11.060 --> 02:12.030
In any case,

02:12.530 --> 02:15.190
I'll draw the first event now.

02:17.074 --> 02:21.714
In any other situation,
I'd say "let's take it easy…"

02:22.740 --> 02:25.360
but give me everything you've got, won't you?

02:27.348 --> 02:29.149
[Event #1: Basketball]

02:37.040 --> 02:41.530
So your strategy is to save
Sudou, your ace, for now.

02:44.170 --> 02:46.740
The rule for this event…

02:46.917 --> 02:51.633
[Special Leader Rule:
You may switch out any one member at any time.]
allows the leader to switch out
one member at any time.

02:51.634 --> 02:51.920
[Special Leader Rule:
You may switch out any one member at any time.]

02:52.640 --> 02:53.840
I see.

03:14.120 --> 03:16.840
They're holding their own even without Sudou.

03:17.500 --> 03:20.190
How odd. They seem unfazed.

03:24.780 --> 03:26.700
I'm invoking the leader rule.

03:27.110 --> 03:31.750
I'll switch out Hondou Ryoutarou for Sudou Ken.

03:33.150 --> 03:36.220
I suspected you'd see through this much.

03:36.900 --> 03:38.590
Otherwise…

03:44.880 --> 03:49.760
What's the matter? Even a novice
like me is too much for you to handle?

03:50.140 --> 03:52.900
You bastard, you've played before, haven't you?!

03:57.730 --> 04:00.000
You were holding back this whole time!

04:01.500 --> 04:04.410
Afraid not. Looks like you just suck.

04:04.790 --> 04:06.740
You dunno who you're messing with!

04:10.520 --> 04:14.900
All it takes to break Sudou is
a little psychological interference.

04:15.340 --> 04:19.579
It doesn't matter how good your technique is,
if your mind is still immature…

04:19.670 --> 04:20.779
Immature?

04:21.829 --> 04:23.890
When did you hear that?

04:25.960 --> 04:29.650
You handed us the lead when
you showed up, basketball boy.

04:29.840 --> 04:32.230
The hell? What's your problem?!

04:32.260 --> 04:33.630
What a simpleton.

04:35.410 --> 04:36.020
Kanji!

04:41.180 --> 04:42.680
That's our Sudou!

04:42.710 --> 04:44.370
Onodera! Nice shot!

04:44.390 --> 04:45.470
There's still time!

04:45.490 --> 04:47.770
Ike and Sudou are in perfect sync.

04:50.480 --> 04:52.560
The winner is Class C.

04:52.760 --> 04:54.540
Hell yeah!

04:54.570 --> 04:56.210
We did it, guys!

04:57.380 --> 04:58.700
Interesting.

04:59.120 --> 05:02.170
So he's shown some growth, I see.

05:03.990 --> 05:05.720
Nice work, guys!

05:05.740 --> 05:07.350
We beat Class A!

05:07.430 --> 05:08.689
[3x3 Basketball - Class C]

05:08.690 --> 05:09.680
[3x3 Basketball - Class C]
That said,

05:10.400 --> 05:14.070
Sudou is a strong card, and we've
already played it this early on.

05:14.380 --> 05:15.390
Second event…

05:15.690 --> 05:15.999
[Event #2: Typing Test]

05:16.000 --> 05:17.900
[Event #2: Typing Test]
Typing test.

05:17.901 --> 05:18.193
[Event #2: Typing Test]

05:18.590 --> 05:21.770
Another of Class C's proposals, hmm.

05:22.330 --> 05:25.010
It seems luck is smiling on you.

05:25.457 --> 05:27.960
[Event #2: Typing Test]

05:33.450 --> 05:37.460
[Event #3: English Test]

05:37.610 --> 05:41.960
[Class C Entrants:
Inogashira, Shinohara, Satou, Karuizawa]

05:45.971 --> 05:49.969
[Event #4: Math Test]

05:49.970 --> 05:54.470
[Class C Entrants:
Yukimura, Hirata, Wang, Kushida]

05:54.470 --> 05:59.980
[Event #5: Archery]

06:00.986 --> 06:03.480
[Class C Entrant:
Miyake]

06:03.900 --> 06:05.390
Not bad at all.

06:05.508 --> 06:05.609
[3x3 Basketball - Class C; Typing - Class C
English - Class A
Math - Class A; Archery - Class C]

06:05.610 --> 06:06.790
[3x3 Basketball - Class C; Typing - Class C
English - Class A
Math - Class A; Archery - Class C]
We need one more win!

06:06.791 --> 06:07.742
[3x3 Basketball - Class C; Typing - Class C
English - Class A
Math - Class A; Archery - Class C]
Just a little more!

06:07.743 --> 06:08.340
Just a little more!

06:08.341 --> 06:11.630
We're winning handily at
the events we proposed ourselves.

06:12.020 --> 06:15.850
Which means, it all depends on what's drawn next…

06:16.030 --> 06:18.369
Now, for the next event…

06:18.370 --> 06:19.620
[Event #6: Mental Arithmetic]

06:19.720 --> 06:21.390
It's one of theirs!

06:21.420 --> 06:23.790
Please choose which students will compete.

06:24.340 --> 06:27.720
We simply can't afford to lose this one.

06:28.470 --> 06:30.180
For this event,

06:30.930 --> 06:35.890
we'd like to call Tamiya Emi and Katsuragi Kouhei.

06:36.410 --> 06:37.330
Yes!

06:37.740 --> 06:40.080
We'll call Matsushita Chiaki,

06:40.710 --> 06:42.460
and Kouenji Rokusuke.

06:43.230 --> 06:45.850
[Event #6: Mental Arithmetic]
The winner is determined by the highest scorer,

06:45.851 --> 06:46.140
[Event #6: Mental Arithmetic]

06:46.140 --> 06:49.820
[Event #6: Mental Arithmetic]
not the class's overall score.

06:49.821 --> 06:50.118
[Event #6: Mental Arithmetic]

06:50.730 --> 06:53.290
So if Kouenji doesn't take it seriously,

06:53.430 --> 06:56.250
your plan is to use Matsushita to cover for him.

06:56.680 --> 06:58.570
The test consists of ten problems.

06:59.040 --> 07:03.140
They will increase in difficulty
and points available as you go.

07:03.910 --> 07:05.040
Now, let's begin.

07:07.636 --> 07:09.638
[Problem #1]

07:12.180 --> 07:13.480
Wait, what?!

07:13.500 --> 07:14.630
There's no way!

07:14.650 --> 07:16.320
That's way too fast!

07:24.900 --> 07:27.900
That damn Kouenji isn't even trying!

07:27.970 --> 07:29.530
Kouenji…

07:30.158 --> 07:30.680
[End of Test]

07:30.680 --> 07:32.630
[End of Test]
That's all ten problems.

07:32.640 --> 07:34.400
[End of Test]
Time's up.

07:34.401 --> 07:34.663
[End of Test]

07:34.860 --> 07:38.110
Wasn't that last one practically impossible?

07:38.590 --> 07:39.450
Well,

07:39.720 --> 07:44.520
the rules state that the leader may
provide the answer to one problem.

07:44.673 --> 07:44.917
[End of Test]

07:44.918 --> 07:46.972
[Select a problem to answer.]
I'd like to answer #10.

07:46.973 --> 07:47.470
[Enter your answer here.]
I'd like to answer #10.

07:47.471 --> 07:47.990
[Enter your answer here.]

07:47.990 --> 07:49.678
[Enter your answer here.]
What about you, Ayanokouji?

07:49.679 --> 07:49.920
[Select a problem to answer.]

07:49.920 --> 07:50.512
[Select a problem to answer.]
Same here.

07:50.513 --> 07:51.340
[Enter your answer here.]
Same here.

07:51.341 --> 07:51.930
[Enter your answer here.]

07:54.660 --> 07:58.590
That was my first try, but it's a fun little game.

07:59.590 --> 08:01.840
The answer to the last question

08:02.100 --> 08:05.210
is 7,619, is it not?

08:05.630 --> 08:07.370
My, oh my.

08:07.490 --> 08:09.130
What a surprise.

08:10.850 --> 08:12.980
I have the results.

08:13.340 --> 08:16.500
In first place, Katsuragi Kouhei.

08:16.740 --> 08:18.790
The winner is Class A.

08:19.800 --> 08:20.890
Damn…

08:21.500 --> 08:24.810
I had a little chat with Katsuragi ahead of time.

08:25.210 --> 08:31.240
I told him that, should he betray me, I'd be happy
to expel a hard-working student from Class A.

08:33.221 --> 08:36.224
[Matsushita Chiaki]
[Kouenji Rokusuke]
[Katsuragi Kouhei]
[Tamiya Emi]

08:40.490 --> 08:44.010
How kind of Kouenji to slack off.

08:44.230 --> 08:48.480
I can't factor an uncontrollable
asset into my plans.

08:48.570 --> 08:49.810
How right you are.

08:50.540 --> 08:53.360
The score is three against three now.

08:53.880 --> 08:57.610
You've caught up, but you
don't look very happy about it.

08:57.890 --> 09:03.070
Just one more event, and the fun will all be over.

09:06.610 --> 09:07.790
And now…

09:08.420 --> 09:12.170
It's time for the seventh and final event.

09:12.950 --> 09:14.760
[Event #7: Chess]

09:15.370 --> 09:18.370
Who could have imagined this would be chosen last?

09:18.510 --> 09:18.639
[Special Leader Rule:
You may provide instructions
for up to 30 minutes in total.]

09:18.640 --> 09:22.210
[Special Leader Rule:
You may provide instructions
for up to 30 minutes in total.]
The rules allow the leader to
give instructions for 30 minutes.

09:22.211 --> 09:23.390
[Special Leader Rule:
You may provide instructions
for up to 30 minutes in total.]
Which means…

09:23.391 --> 09:23.530
[Special Leader Rule:
You may provide instructions
for up to 30 minutes in total.]

09:23.530 --> 09:26.440
[Special Leader Rule:
You may provide instructions
for up to 30 minutes in total.]
this is a battle of skill between you and me.

09:26.960 --> 09:30.440
Sorry to break it to you, but I'm good at chess.

09:30.800 --> 09:32.650
My, my, my.

09:33.160 --> 09:34.630
What a coincidence.

09:35.030 --> 09:40.030
[Classroom of the Elite
3rd Season]

09:47.920 --> 09:50.520
He is our finest test subject.

09:51.160 --> 09:55.690
Still, I can't help but pity him.

09:56.410 --> 09:57.730
Why is that?

09:57.970 --> 10:01.930
He's lived in this facility since
the very moment he was born.

10:02.110 --> 10:04.020
He knows nothing of parental love,

10:04.200 --> 10:06.670
nor the warmth of human touch.

10:37.420 --> 10:38.470
[Final Exam Event #7: Chess]

10:42.450 --> 10:45.810
We will now begin the final round.

11:01.360 --> 11:04.140
I've only been learning chess for a couple months,

11:04.380 --> 11:06.100
so go easy on me.

11:06.610 --> 11:10.310
I'm sorry to hear that.
I've been learning for a week.

11:11.680 --> 11:16.250
You won't be going up against anyone harder
than me when I'm going easy on you.

11:19.240 --> 11:20.770
I wonder why…

11:21.330 --> 11:22.790
I feel so sure I'll win.

11:40.950 --> 11:43.330
A rebellious little strategy, isn't it?

11:43.460 --> 11:45.610
Courtesy of Sakayanagi, I presume.

11:46.670 --> 11:50.680
I bet you've had a real drill sergeant
whipping you into shape, too, huh?

11:50.760 --> 11:52.570
Well, who's to say?

11:53.250 --> 11:56.260
Well, whatever. Anyway,

11:56.700 --> 11:59.050
can I ask you something about Ayanokouji?

12:00.960 --> 12:03.340
Ever since what happened on the island,

12:03.600 --> 12:08.100
I've been thinking maybe he's the one
pulling the strings behind the scenes.

12:08.340 --> 12:09.940
Based on what, I wonder?

12:10.500 --> 12:12.110
Call it intuition.

12:12.140 --> 12:13.440
Now answer me.

12:13.870 --> 12:15.600
Answer what, exactly?

12:15.970 --> 12:19.040
I don't even know what you're talking about.

12:19.320 --> 12:22.980
Oh, really? You seem a little uneasy, though.

12:23.500 --> 12:26.940
I assumed you'd be trying to throw me off.

12:27.350 --> 12:30.820
But you won't break my resolve that easily.

12:35.080 --> 12:39.180
Are you sure you can afford to
waste energy running your mouth?

12:39.500 --> 12:41.734
This just got a little more interesting.

12:44.500 --> 12:48.540
As much as I'd love to see how
this plays out to the very end…

12:49.060 --> 12:51.550
I think it's about time I stepped in.

12:55.870 --> 12:58.520
Wish I could say I'm doing fine,

12:59.360 --> 13:01.070
but no lie, this is a relief.

13:08.720 --> 13:11.180
This is a massive jump in skill.

13:13.890 --> 13:16.110
You're still not stepping in yet,

13:16.370 --> 13:17.970
Ayanokouji?

13:19.820 --> 13:24.150
I'll go ahead and take the win, then, shall I?

13:26.350 --> 13:28.120
I can't counter this…

13:29.770 --> 13:31.100
Ayanokouji!

13:33.400 --> 13:34.810
It's time.

13:39.480 --> 13:43.450
The two of us can have our battle at last, hmm?

14:05.160 --> 14:07.090
Whoa, what the hell?

14:07.470 --> 14:10.110
How can those two think this fast?

14:11.470 --> 14:15.040
It makes our plays look utterly pathetic.

14:15.420 --> 14:16.450
Seriously.

14:17.210 --> 14:19.550
What's the matter, Ayanokouji?

14:19.740 --> 14:23.810
Are you really feeling that last move?

14:24.110 --> 14:26.360
Yeah, it kind of stings.

14:26.900 --> 14:29.800
One wrong move, and you'll
break through my defenses.

14:30.200 --> 14:32.200
Surely that's not a concern.

14:33.190 --> 14:37.510
I know you won't make any careless mistakes.

14:38.200 --> 14:41.380
In that case, you're free to resign.

14:41.700 --> 14:43.830
That is out of the question.

14:44.030 --> 14:45.680
If there will be no mistakes,

14:45.950 --> 14:48.680
I'll just have to break through by skill alone…

14:55.000 --> 14:57.770
What a delight this is…

15:02.420 --> 15:06.120
But I suppose you're not
one to let it end like this.

15:10.830 --> 15:12.170
I didn't see that!

15:18.030 --> 15:19.540
Listen, Arisu.

15:19.980 --> 15:24.750
If these children grow up to
excel over everyone else,

15:25.280 --> 15:28.400
and this institution's methods become the norm…

15:28.780 --> 15:32.620
I believe it will only lead to suffering.

15:36.030 --> 15:37.590
Don't you worry.

15:37.960 --> 15:41.200
I'll destroy it myself.

15:42.970 --> 15:45.960
You truly are remarkable, Ayanokouji.

15:47.540 --> 15:49.540
I've had a lovely time.

15:50.250 --> 15:54.310
It is a shame it's drawing to a close, but…

15:56.030 --> 15:57.650
this is the end.

16:10.300 --> 16:11.830
Ayanokouji…

16:12.490 --> 16:13.930
I don't want to lose.

16:14.930 --> 16:16.170
I'm still…

16:16.640 --> 16:18.900
not ready to accept defeat.

16:19.330 --> 16:20.420
I want to win!

16:21.430 --> 16:26.460
If there's some way to best her
that I can't conceive of…

16:28.230 --> 16:30.180
you're the only one who would know!

16:35.620 --> 16:36.960
Like this?

16:43.300 --> 16:45.460
Excellent work, Ayanokouji.

16:46.010 --> 16:52.790
Without a doubt, that move is on
a level no ordinary person could reach.

16:53.280 --> 16:57.670
However… I have my own reasons for needing to win.

16:59.530 --> 17:02.480
A person's aptitude is determined at birth.

17:02.890 --> 17:11.460
As someone who inherited superior DNA, allow me
to prove there is no value in that institution.

17:11.859 --> 17:15.290
That is the salvation I strive for.

17:16.460 --> 17:17.560
And…

17:17.930 --> 17:21.030
there is one thing I need you to understand.

17:22.800 --> 17:23.819
Check.

17:45.270 --> 17:47.290
We… lost.

17:47.690 --> 17:50.870
Time's up. The winner is Class A.

17:56.650 --> 17:58.740
What an excellent battle.

17:59.190 --> 18:02.420
It could have been anyone's game,
right to the very end.

18:03.340 --> 18:04.260
And yet…

18:05.360 --> 18:06.400
What is it?

18:06.820 --> 18:08.680
That last move of yours.

18:08.980 --> 18:12.290
Was that really the best move you could think of?

18:12.550 --> 18:14.550
What else would it be?

18:15.540 --> 18:19.060
You really are merciless, Ayanokouji.

18:20.790 --> 18:24.130
Why not tell her the truth?

18:24.690 --> 18:26.260
What are you talking about?

18:26.570 --> 18:32.350
By all rights, that should have been your win.

18:34.000 --> 18:40.810
At the end, you figured out the best move,
and the piece moved one space past it.

18:40.890 --> 18:45.760
Unbelievable… You interfered in our exam.

18:46.930 --> 18:49.610
You changed Ayanokouji's instructions,

18:50.440 --> 18:53.220
and gave Horikita the wrong information.

18:59.760 --> 19:02.600
Why didn't you speak up about this?

19:03.300 --> 19:10.140
Why would he do something that could bring
unwelcome attention to his own situation?

19:11.690 --> 19:13.690
You only have yourself to blame…

19:14.330 --> 19:19.450
for letting Ayanokouji get
his hands on that protection point.

19:20.700 --> 19:24.310
Still, as sad as it is, a win is a win.

19:24.730 --> 19:26.620
Shouldn't you be celebrating?

19:27.050 --> 19:29.200
You're quite the instigator.

19:29.800 --> 19:32.130
You'll pay a high price for this.

19:32.420 --> 19:37.840
Kids really do say the darndest things.

19:39.220 --> 19:41.160
Give it your best shot.

21:18.160 --> 21:20.720
I simply must hand it to you, Ayanokouji.

21:21.220 --> 21:22.760
That was my loss.

21:23.320 --> 21:25.510
It's big of you to admit it.

21:26.160 --> 21:29.970
We picked up from the same
place as before, and I lost.

21:30.320 --> 21:32.920
I can accept that gracefully.

21:33.660 --> 21:40.860
You could have proposed only one-on-one events
for the exam and faced me directly.

21:41.840 --> 21:43.650
Why didn't you?

21:44.440 --> 21:50.290
I didn't want everyone to know
what you're truly capable of.

21:50.890 --> 21:53.410
So you were looking out for me.

21:54.200 --> 21:56.120
I'm glad we got to compete.

21:56.790 --> 22:00.220
Now I have the answer I've been looking for.

22:01.570 --> 22:05.240
You are undeniably a genius.

22:05.870 --> 22:08.440
No one could ever say you're a fake.

22:11.150 --> 22:12.640
You saw me, huh.

22:13.370 --> 22:15.540
When I was in the White Room.

22:15.770 --> 22:19.990
I've been quite fond of chess ever since.

22:20.680 --> 22:24.300
I knew we would have a chance to
play against each other one day.

22:24.720 --> 22:29.950
I was simply desperate to know more about you.

22:30.460 --> 22:32.600
I kept chasing after you,

22:33.200 --> 22:37.940
as if we were old friends,
even though we'd never met.

22:38.910 --> 22:41.660
I owe you an apology, by the way.

22:42.110 --> 22:43.250
An apology?

22:43.300 --> 22:49.580
I was lying when I told you why I
avoided facing off against you directly.

22:52.040 --> 22:58.720
I simply wanted to stay in the same place
with you, for even just a moment longer.

23:01.440 --> 23:05.880
People come to know warmth through touch.

23:06.740 --> 23:09.190
It is a very precious thing.

23:17.210 --> 23:22.020
There is nothing bad about
the warmth of human touch.

23:22.950 --> 23:24.570
I want you to remember that.

23:25.450 --> 23:26.930
What do you mean?

23:27.860 --> 23:31.570
It's a message I've given to you far too late.

23:36.500 --> 23:39.090
Let's head back, shall we?
